## 5. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Pod `ErrImageNeverPull` | The image wasn't imported into containerd, or the tag in the manifest has a typo | Re-run phase 5 and check with the kubectl image list; compare against the manifest tag |
| Phase 6 says `MISSING on node` | The import didn't run, or imported into the wrong containerd namespace | The import must use `-n k8s.io`; re-run phase 5 |
| Image missing from the node list, but the import printed `saved` | The kubelet hasn't refreshed the list yet, or the node has more than 50 images | Wait a minute; confirm with `sudo k3s crictl images \| grep <tag>`; remove old images (phase 8); if needed, use `SKIP_NODE_CHECK=1` |
| `kubectl apply` reports `configured` for a deployment outside the release (e.g. `proxy`) | Only metadata changed (the last-applied annotation) | Nothing to do if the pod's `CREATED` time didn't change |
| New route returns HTML titled "CSRF Verification Failed" | Expected for a POST without a session or CSRF token | The route is deployed; test it from the UI |
| Feature email (2FA code, invite) never arrives | SMTP isn't set in god-mode, or the worker isn't running or is failing | God-mode → Email → **Send test email**; `kubectl -n plane logs deploy/worker --since=10m` |
| Phase 6 says `tag not set for <c>` | The manifest uses a non-standard image name | Rename it to `cybernetics-project-<c>:<anything>` in the manifest, then re-run |
| New endpoint returns `{"error": "Page not found."}` | The backend image wasn't updated, or the route isn't registered in `apps/api/plane/api/urls/__init__.py` | Check `kubectl -n plane get deploy api -o wide`; check URL registration |
| Migrator Job fails | A broken migration, or the database is unreachable | `kubectl -n plane logs job/migrator`; the app pods are untouched, so fix and re-run |
| `rollout status` times out | The new pod is crash-looping | `kubectl -n plane describe pod -l app=<deploy>` and `kubectl -n plane logs deploy/<deploy> --previous` |
| UI calls fail with CORS errors | `WEB_URL` / `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in `plane-config` don't match `https://projects.avarile.com` | Fix `configmap.yaml`, `kubectl apply -k`, then `kubectl -n plane rollout restart deploy` |
| MCP returns 401 | The token was revoked or has expired | Create a new token in Profile → API tokens |
| MCP has fewer tools than expected | `MCP_READ_ONLY=1`, or `MCP_TOOLSETS` limits the groups in `plane-config` | Check `kubectl -n plane get cm plane-config -o yaml \| grep MCP_` |
| Phase 4 is slow or stalls | Upload bandwidth to the server | Ship fewer components; zstd level `-3` is a good balance (`-19` is much slower) |
| `kubectl diff` shows unexpected other changes | Someone edited live objects or the repo without applying | Review `kubectl diff -k apps/plane/` before the real rollout; commit or revert the drift |

Useful commands on the server:

```bash
kubectl -n plane get deploy -o wide                     # images per deployment
kubectl -n plane get pods -o wide
kubectl -n plane logs deploy/api --tail=100 -f           # API (JSON logs; MCP lines have name "mcp.*" / "plane.mcp")
kubectl -n plane logs deploy/worker --tail=100
kubectl -n plane get cm plane-config -o yaml             # non-secret config (MCP_*, WEB_URL, …)
ls ~/plane-releases/                                     # rollback points
```

